    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "Douz, the 'Gateway to the Sahara', is the epicenter of desert adventure and traditional nomadic culture in Tunisia. It is world-renowned for its annual International Festival of the Sahara, which celebrates desert life, camel racing, and local Berber traditions. The city borders the vast Grand Erg Oriental dunes, making it a critical point for Saharan expeditions and desert tourism. Douz offers an authentic glimpse into the lives of those who have historically navigated the vast Tunisian dunes. Geography K7: The cultural significance of desert festivals and tourism as an economic driver for borderland Saharan cities."
    },
