    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "Sbeitla is home to some of the best-preserved Roman ruins in Tunisia, known as the site of ancient Sufetula. The city’s archaeological park features spectacular triumphal arches, temples, and theaters that testify to its historical prominence as a wealthy inland center. Today, Sbeitla is a growing city that balances its rich archaeological assets with a developing agricultural and service economy. It serves as an essential destination for anyone wanting to understand the Roman footprint on the Tunisian landscape. Geography K8: Analyzing the preservation of historical archaeological assets within modern inland urban developments."
    },
