    descriptionAdvanced: {
      en: "Carthage is an iconic historical metropolis that once stood as the rival of Rome and a dominant maritime power in the Mediterranean. Today, it is an upscale suburb of Tunis, where modern villas blend with spectacular Punic and Roman archaeological ruins. The site is a UNESCO World Heritage area, attracting visitors eager to walk through history, from the Punic ports to the Antonine Baths. Carthage remains a symbol of North African maritime ambition and enduring historical legacy. Geography K6: The rise and fall of ancient maritime empires and their impact on modern landscape patterns."
    },
